No, no, no!  Trying to catch a unicorn by using Ctrl-T will NOT work!!
When you teleport by typing ^T (or, for that matter, by reading a teleport
scroll or casting a teleport spell), you use up your move to do so.  This
means after you teleport, the unicorn will get a free move so that it can
move/teleport out of your line of sight.
   The ONLY way to get in line-of-fire with a unicorn is to have intrinsic
teleportation (or wear a ring of teleportation).  Then, when a teleport
"descends" on you from out of the blue, you can decide where you wish to
end up WITHOUT letting the unicorn get an extra move.
   Of course, doing this twice with two identified gems (even jade will do)
will raise your luck to max, so this shouldn't take too long.

